course: dictionary
lesson: 7180
title: Personal: about one person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Personal has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. It can mean belonging to or about one particular person. «Philosophers call this the question of personal identity» means the question of who one single person really is.
explain: Personal can also mean private, about your own life, body or feelings. «A diary is personal and chatty» means a diary holds your own private thoughts. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a single person, a secret, a feeling, or something you did yourself.
explain: Personal can mean done by you yourself, not through someone else. In «Who's making personal remarks now?», the Hatter means comments aimed at a particular person, which can be unkind. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Personal means belonging to or about one particular person.
fact: Personal means private, about your own life, body or feelings.
fact: Personal means done by you yourself, not through someone else.
fact: In online safety, keep personal information private: your full name, address, school, phone number, passwords and photos.
fact: A personal best (PB) is your own fastest or highest result in sport.
exercise: «A diary is personal and chatty.» What does personal mean here? | Shared with the whole school | Written by a machine | Very expensive | *Private, about your own thoughts and life
exercise: Sam says, «Keep your personal information safe online.» Which of these is personal information? | A score from a football match on TV | The weather forecast for Friday | The name of a famous city | *Your home address
exercise: «Who's making personal remarks now?» asks the Hatter. What are personal remarks? | Long lists of facts about the weather | Remarks that are always praise | Notes sent to the whole class | *Comments aimed at a particular person, often unkind
test: «Philosophers call this the question of personal identity.» What does personal identity mean? | *Who one particular person really is | Where a person lives | The identity card a school gives out | A group of people working together
test: Ella set a personal best in the 100 metres. What is a personal best? | Her team's fastest time | The best time anyone has ever run | *Her own fastest or highest result | A prize for coming first
exam: Politics feels most personal when a decision touches your own job, like nurses' pay. Why does politics feel personal here? | Because politics is always about one person | *Because it is about your own job and life | Because a nurse wrote the law | Because it happens in private
